      "comment": "PRINCE OF POP (6) is a work in progress having made mistakes in his last two outings but he is in a good yard and there looks to be some ability there. The only time he got it right he finished fourth at Goulburn. Winning chance if the penny drops. LITTLE MISS MINNIE (3) hasn't raced since a modest eighth on debut four-and-a-half months ago but a recent trial win suggests she has developed since and she is aided by a good draw. BOOMER SHANNON (5) was returning from a layoff here last time out when he settled back from a second line draw but made up plenty of ground to finish third. The long-time maiden tag is a worry but he should be fitter. NAVARLIES DREAM (1) had a tough draw last start but was fourth from this barrier prior so is better served tonight.",
